.DS_Store
node_modules/

# Gauntlet scratch. `tools/gauntlet/*.mjs` regenerate every one of these on
# demand, so the renders, blind comparisons and round files are output, not
# source. The final contact sheet is kept because it is the artefact the pass
# is judged on.
tools/gauntlet/*.png
!tools/gauntlet/contact-final.png
tools/gauntlet/*.json
tools/gauntlet/fixtures/
tools/gauntlet/reverted/

# Mixamo source downloads. 200MB of FBX, and the same argument as node_modules:
# they are inputs re-fetchable from mixamo.com, not source. What the game ships
# is baked out of them — `js/clips/*.js` and the sheets in `art/` — and those
# are committed, so a clone runs without them. Re-download only to re-bake.
art/mixamo/

# Doll and mocap renders. `tools/bake-doll.mjs` and `tools/doll.html` regenerate
# every one on demand, the same reason tools/gauntlet/*.png is ignored above.
tools/gauntlet/mocap/

# VFX source. ProRes clips and the Kenney particle pack are inputs, like
# art/mixamo/ — what ships is baked out of them by tools/vfx-sheet.swift and
# committed as art/vfx-*.png.
art/vfx/

# Character kits. Quaternius' Modular Character Outfits (bought) and Universal
# Base Characters (free), both CC0, and both the same argument as art/mixamo/
# above: 900MB of inputs, not source. What the game ships is baked out of them
# by tools/outfit.py and committed as art/knight-*.png, so a clone runs without
# them. Re-download only to re-bake.
Modular Character Outfits - Fantasy\[Source\]/
Universal Base Characters\[Standard\]/
*.zip

# The GLBs those kits are assembled into. Intermediates between the kit and the
# sheet — regenerated by `blender --background --python tools/outfit.py` — and
# 23MB of them. The sheets are the artefact; these are the working file.
art/armour/
